    "Surahs of the Night\nSecond: On Friday nights it is recommended to recite the following chapters (Surahs) of the Holy Qur'an:\n(1) [Surah al-Isra](A21) (No. 17), (2) [Surah al-Kahf](A22) (No. 18), (3) the three Surahs beginning with Ta-Sin, i.e. [Surah al-Shu'ara](A30) (No. 26), [Surah al-Naml](A31) (No. 27) and [Surah al-Qasas](A32) (No. 28), (4) [Surah al-Sajdah](A36) (No. 32), (5) [Surah Ya-Sin](A40) (No. 36), (6) [Surah Sad](A42) (No. 38), (7) [Surah al-Ahqaf](A50) (No. 46), (8) [Surah al-Waqi'ah](A60) (No. 56), (9) [Surah Fussilat](A45) (No. 41), (10) [Surah al-Dukhan](A48) (No. 44), (11) [Surah al-Tur](A56) (No. 52), (12) [Surah al-Qamar](A58) (No. 54), and (13) [Surah al-Jumu'ah](A66) (No. 62).\nIf there is not enough time to recite all these Surahs, one may choose Surah al-Waqi'ah and those preceding it in the list above.\nImam al-Sadiq (a.s.) is reported to have said that one who recites Surah al-Isra' every Friday night will join Imam al-Mahdi (a.t.f.s.) as one of his companions; that one who recites Surah al-Kahf on Friday nights will die a martyr and will be resurrected with the martyrs; and that one who recites the three Surahs beginning with Ta-Sin on Friday nights will be among the intimate servants of Almighty Allah, in His vicinity and under His protection, will never be afflicted with misery in this world, and will be given beyond his pleasure on the Day of Resurrection.\nHe (a.s.) is also reported to have said that one who recites Surah al-Sajdah on Friday nights will be given his Record of Deeds in his right hand, will not be called to account for his evildoings, and will be included with the companions of Muhammad and his Household (a.s.).\nImam Muhammad al-Baqir (a.s.) is authentically reported to have said that one who recites Surah Sad on Friday nights will be granted the good of this world and the Hereafter as none but the Prophets and the archangels are given, and will be admitted to Paradise together with all those of his household whom he loves, including his servants.\nImam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a.s.) is reported to have said that one who recites Surah al-Ahqaf on Fridays or on Friday nights will be saved by Almighty Allah from terror in this world and will be secured from the horror of the Day of Resurrection; and that one who recites Surah al-Waqi'ah on Friday nights will be loved by Almighty Allah and by all people, will be saved from all misery, poverty, need and misfortune in this world, and will be among the companions of Amir al-Mu'minin (a.s.), because this Surah belongs to him.\nIt has also been narrated that reciting Surah al-Jumu'ah on Friday nights is an expiation for the sins committed during the week. A similar merit has been narrated for reciting Surah al-Kahf on Friday nights, or after the Zuhr and Asr Prayers on Fridays.",
    "Prayers and Other Acts of the Night\nIt is highly recommended to offer many supererogatory prayers on Friday nights, such as the [Prayer of Amir al-Mu'minin (a.s.)](F15), and a two-unit prayer in each unit of which one recites [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Zalzalah](A103) fifteen times. It has been narrated that one who offers this prayer will be saved by Almighty Allah from the torment of the grave and the horrors of the Day of Resurrection.\nThird: It is recommended to recite [Surah al-Jumu'ah](A66) in the first unit of the Maghrib and Isha obligatory prayers, [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) in the second unit of the Maghrib Prayer, and [Surah al-A'la](A91) in the second unit of the Isha Prayer.\nFourth: It is highly recommended to avoid reciting poetry on Friday nights. Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a.s.) is authentically reported to have said that it is disliked to recite poetry for one who is fasting, for one in the state of ihram, and on Fridays and Friday nights; when asked whether this applies to religiously acceptable poetry too, the Imam (a.s.) answered that it does. It has also been authentically narrated from Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) that the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said, \"One who recites even one verse of poetry on a Friday or a Friday night will have no share of reward on it except for that poetry.\" According to another narration, the prayers of those who recite poetry on Fridays will not be accepted.\nFifth: It is highly recommended to pray to Almighty Allah very frequently for the good of one's brethren-in-faith, following the example of Lady Fatimah al-Zahra (s.a.). According to a hadith, one who prays for ten deceased believers will certainly be admitted to Paradise.\nIt is also recommended, following Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a.s.), to eat a pomegranate on Friday nights, preferably before going to sleep. It has been narrated that eating a pomegranate before sleeping brings security until the morning. It is also instructive to spread a cloth on the ground so as to save every seed of the pomegranate and eat them all, and it is recommended not to share it with anyone.\nSixth: It is also recommended to say the supplications dedicated to Friday nights. They are too numerous to be cited here; a few of them follow in the next tabs.",
    "Dua in the Last Prostration of the Isha Nafilah\nImam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a.s.) is authentically reported as saying that one who says the following dua seven times in the last prostration of the supererogatory (nafilah) prayer of Isha on Friday nights will have all his sins forgiven as soon as he finishes that prayer. It is desirable to do this every night.\nاَللَّهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَسْاَلُكَ بِوَجْهِكَ الْكَريمِ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUKA BIWAJHIKAL KAREEM\nO Allah, I beseech You in the name of Your Noble Face\nوَاسْمِكَ الْعَظيمِ\nWASMIKAL A'ZEEM\nand in the name of Your Sublime Name\nاَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلَىٰ مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِهٖ\nAN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\nto send blessings to Muhammad and his Household\nوَاَنْ تَغْفِرَ لِي ذَنْبِيَ الْعَظيمَ\nWA AN TAGHFIRA LEE DHANBIYAL A'ZEEM\nand to forgive me my grave sin.",
    "Dua Allahumma Anta Rabbi\nThe Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) is reported to have said that one who repeats the following supplication seven times on a Friday night will be admitted to Paradise if he dies that night, and one who repeats it seven times on Friday will be admitted to Paradise if he dies that day.\nاَللَّهُمَّ اَنْتَ رَبِّيْ\nALLAAHUMMA ANTA RABBEE\nO Allah, You are my Lord;\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANT\nthere is no god save You;\nخَلَقْتَنِيْ وَاَنَا عَبْدُكَ وَابْنُ اَمَتِكَ\nKHALAQTANEE WA ANAA A'BDUKA WABNU AMATIK\nYou have created me, and I am Your slave and the son of Your bondmaid;\nوَفِيْ قَبْضَتِكَ وَنَاصِيَتي بِيَدِكَ\nWA FEE QABDATIKA WA NAASIYATEE BIYADIK\nand I am in Your grip; and my forehead is in Your Hand;\nاَمْسَيْتُ عَلَىٰ عَهْدِكَ وَوَعْدِكَ مَا اسْتَطَعْتُ\nAMSAYTU A'LAA A'HDIKA WA WA'DIKA MAS TATA'T\nI come to observe my covenant and promise to You as much as I can.\nاَعُوْذُ بِرِضَاكَ مِنْ شَرِّ مَا صَنَعْتُ\nA'OODHU BIRIDAAKA MIN SHARRI MAA SANA'T\nI take refuge in Your pleasure against the evil of my deeds.\nاَبُوءُ بِنِعْمَتِكَ وَاَبُوءُ بِذَنْبِيْ\nABOO'U BINI'MATIKA WA ABOO'U BIDHANBEE\nI acknowledge Your favors and confess of my sins.\nفَاغْفِرْ لِيْ ذُنُوْبِيْ\nFAGHFIR LEE DHUNOOBEE\nSo, (please) forgive my sins,\nاِنَّهٗ لَا يَغْفِرُ الذُّنُوبَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ\nINNAHOO LAA YAGHFIRUDH DHUNOOBA ILLAA ANT\nfor none can forgive sins save You.",
    "Dua Allahumma Man Ta'abba'a\nShaykh al-Tusi, Sayyid Ibn Tawus, al-Kaf'ami and Sayyid Ibn Baqi have recorded that it is recommended to say the following supplication on Fridays and Friday nights, and on the day and night of Arafah (the ninth of Dhul Hijjah). It is cited here as given in Shaykh al-Tusi's al-Misbah.\nاَللَّهُمَّ مَنْ تَعَبَّاَ وَتَهَيَّاَ\nALLAAHUMMA MAN TA'ABBA'A WA TAHAYYA'\nO Allah, One may call up, prepare,\nوَاَعَدَّ وَاسْتَعَدَّ\nWA A'ADDA WASTA'ADD\nready oneself, and stand prepared\nلِوِفَادَةٍ اِلَىٰ مَخْلُوْقٍ\nLIWIFAADATIN ILAA MAKHLOOQ\nfor purpose of coming to a creature\nرَجَاءَ رِفْدِهٖ\nRAJAA'A RIFDIH\nin the hope of gaining his aid\nوَطَلَبَ نَائِلِهٖ وَجَائِزَتِهٖ\nWA TALABA NAA'ILIHEE WA JAA'IZATIH\nand asking for his gift and present.\nفَاِلَيْكَ يَا رَبِّ تَعْبِيَتِيْ وَاسْتِعْدَادِي\nFA-ILAYKA YAA RABBI TA'BIYATEE WASTI'DAADEE\nAs for myself, to You—O my Lord—I make my preparations and readiness\nرَجَاءَ عَفْوِكَ\nRAJAA'A A'FWIK\nhoping for Your pardon\nوَطَلَبَ نَائِلِكَ وَجَائِزَتِكَ\nWA TALABA NAA'ILIKA WA JAA'IZATIK\nand asking for Your gift and present.\nفَلَا تُخَيِّبْ دُعَاۤئِي\nFALAA TUKHAYYIB DU'AA'EE\nSo, (please) do not disappoint my entreaty.\nيَا مَنْ لَا يَخِيْبُ عَلَيْهِ سَائِلٌ\nYAA MAN LAA YAKHEEBU A'LAYHI SAA'IL\nO He Who never disappoints His beseechers\nوَلَا يَنْقُصُهٗ نَائِلٌ\nWA LAA YANQUSUHOO NAA'IL\nand Whose prizes never decrease His ample-giving!\nفَاِنِّيْ لَمْ اٰتِكَ ثِقَةً بِعَمَلٍ صَالِحٍ عَمِلْتُهٗ\nFA-INNEE LAM AATIKA THIQATAN BI-A'MALIN SAALIHIN A'MILTUH\nI have not come to You with confidence of a righteous deed that I have done\nوَلَا لِوِفَادَةِ مَخْلُوْقٍ رَجَوْتُهٗ\nWA LAA LIWIFAADATI MAKHLOOQIN RAJAWTUH\nnor have I had any hope in a grant of any creature.\nاَتَيْتُكَ مُقِرّاً عَلَىٰ نَفْسِيْ بِالْاِسَاءَةِ وَالظُّلْمِ\nATAYTUKA MUQIRRAN A'LAA NAFSEE BIL ISAA'ATI WAZ ZULM\nRather, I have come to You professing myself to be evildoer and transgressor\nمُعْتَرِفاً بِاَنْ لَّا حُجَّةَ لِيْ وَلَا عُذْرَ\nMU'TARIFAN BI-AL LAA HUJJATA LEE WA LAA U'DHR\nand confessing that I lack any pretext or excuse.\nاَتَيْتُكَ اَرْجُوْ عَظِيْمَ عَفْوِكَ\nATAYTUKA ARJOO A'ZEEMA A'FWIK\nI have come to You hoping for Your great pardon\nالَّذِي عَفَوْتَ بِهٖ عَنِ الْخَاطِئينَ\nALLADHEE A'FAWTA BIHEE A'NIL KHAATI'EEN\ndue to which You have pardoned the wrongdoers.\nفَلَمْ يَمْنَعْكَ طُوْلُ عُكُوْفِهِمْ عَلِي عَظِيْمِ الْجُرْمِ\nFALAM YAMNA'KA TOOLU U'KOOFIHIM A'LEE A'ZEEMIL JURM\nHence, their long-lasting retirement to their grave offenses has not prevented You\nاَنْ عُدْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ بِالرَّحْمَةِ\nAN U'DTA A'LAYHIM BIR RAHMAH\nfrom turning to them with mercy.\nفَيَا مَنْ رَحْمَتُهٗ وَاسِعَةٌ\nFAYAA MAN RAHMATUHOO WAASI'AH\nO He Whose mercy is huge\nوَعَفْوُهٗ عَظِيْمٌ\nWA A'FWUHOO A'ZEEM\nand Whose pardon is great;\nيَا عَظِيمُ يَا عَظِيمُ يَا عَظِيمُ\nYAA A'ZEEMU YAA A'ZEEMU YAA A'ZEEM\nO All-great, O All-great, O All-great;\nلَا يَرُدُّ غَضَبَكَ اِلَّا حِلْمُكَ\nLAA YARUDDU GHADABAKA ILLAA HILMUK\nnothing can repel Your rage except Your forbearance\nوَلَا يُنْجِيْ مِنْ سَخَطِكَ اِلَّا التَّضَرُّعُ اِلَيْكَ\nWA LAA YUNJEE MIN SAKHATIKA ILLAT TADARRU'U ILAYK\nand nothing can save from Your wrath except imploring earnestly to You.\nفَهَبْ لِيْ يَا اِلٰهِي فَرَجاً\nFAHAB LEE YAA ILAAHEE FARAJAA\nSo, my God, (please) grant me a relief\nبِالْقُدْرَةِ الَّتِي تُحْيِيْ بِهَا مَيْتَ الْبِلَادِ\nBIL QUDRATIL LATEE TUHYEE BIHAA MAYTAL BILAAD\nin the name of the power through which You restore to life the derelict lands,\nوَلَا تُهْلِكْنِيْ غَمّاً حَتَّىٰ تَسْتَجِيْبَ لِيْ\nWA LAA TUHLIKNEE GHAMMAN HATTAA TASTAJEEBA LEE\nand do not cause me to perish out of grief until You respond to me\nوَتُعَرِّفَنِي الْاِجَابَةَ فِي دُعَائِي\nWA TU'ARRIFANIL IJAABATA FEE DU'AA'EE\nand show me signs of Your response to my prayers.\nوَاَذِقْنِي طَعْمَ الْعَافِيَةِ اِلَىٰ مُنْتَهٰى اَجَلِيْ\nWA ADHIQNEE TA'MAL A'AFIYATI ILAA MUNTAHAA AJALEE\n(please) Make me taste the flavor of wellbeing up to the end of my lifetime,\nوَلَا تُشْمِتْ بِيْ عَدُوِّيْ\nWA LAA TUSHMIT BEE A'DUWWEE\ndo not make my enemies gloat over me,\nوَلَا تُسَلِّطْهُ عَلَيَّ\nWA LAA TUSALLIT-HU A'LAYY\ndo not give them a hand over me,\nوَلَا تُمَكِّنْهُ مِنْ عُنُقِيْ\nWA LAA TUMAKKINHU MIN U'NUQEE\nand do not make them control over me.\nاَللَّهُمَّ اِنْ وَضَعْتَنِيْ فَمَنْ ذَا الَّذِي يَرْفَعُنِي\nALLAAHUMMA IN WADA'TANEE FAMAN DHAL LADHEE YARFA'UNEE\nO Allah, If You humiliate me, who can then exalt me?\nوَاِنْ رَفَعْتَنِيْ فَمَنْ ذَا الَّذِي يَضَعُنِيْ\nWA IN RAFA'TANEE FAMAN DHAL LADHEE YADA'UNEE\nAnd if You exalt me, who can then humiliate me?\nوَاِنْ اَهْلَكْتَنِيْ فَمَنْ ذَا الَّذِي يَعْرِضُ لَكَ فِي عَبْدِكَ\nWA IN AHLAKTANEE FAMAN DHAL LADHEE YA'RIDU LAKA FEE A'BDIK\nIf You annihilate me, who can then interfere before You concerning the affair of me—Your slave\nاَوْ يَسْاَلُكَ عَنْ اَمْرِهٖ،\nAW YAS'ALUKA A'N AMRIH\nor who can intercede to ask You about it?\nوَقَدْ عَلِمْتُ اَنَّهٗ لَيْسَ فِي حُكْمِكَ ظُلْمٌ\nWA QAD A'LIMTU ANNAHOO LAYSA FEE HUKMIKA ZULM\nI have already known for sure that Your decrees are devoid of injustice\nوَلَا فِي نَقَمَتِكَ عَجَلَةٌ\nWA LAA FEE NAQAMATIKA A'JALAH\nand Your punishment does not count on immediateness.\nوَاِنَّمَا يَعْجَلُ مَنْ يَخَافُ الْفَوْتَ\nWA INNAMAA YA'JALU MAN YAKHAAFUL FAWT\nVerily, immediateness is the work of him who fears lest he may miss,\nوَاِنَّمَا يَحْتَاجُ اِلَىٰ الظُّلْمِ الضَّعِيفُ\nWA INNAMAA YAHTAAJU ILAZ ZULMID DA'EEF\nand only do the weak need injustice.\nوَقَدْ تَعَالَيْتَ يَا اِلٰهِي عَنْ ذٰلِكَ عُلُوّاً كَبِيراً\nWA QAD TA'AALAYTA YAA ILAAHEE A'N DHAALIKA U'LUWWAN KABEERAA\nAs for You, O my God, You are too exalted to be so—Exalted and Great You are beyond all measure!\nاَللَّهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ فَاَعِذْنِيْ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE A'OODHU BIKA FA-A'IDHNEE\nO Allah, I take refuge in You; so, (please) have protection upon me!\nوَاَسْتَجِيرُ بِكَ فَاَجِرْنِيْ\nWA ASTAJEERU BIKA FA-AJIRNEE\nI call for Your safekeeping; so, (please) keep me under Your security!\nوَاَسْتَرْزِقُكَ فَارْزُقْنِيْ\nWA ASTARZIQUKA FARZUQNEE\nI appeal for Your sustenance; so, (please) provide me with sustenance!\nوَاَتَوَكَّلُ عَلَيْكَ فَاكْفِنِيْ\nWA ATAWAKKALU A'LAYKA FAKFINEE\nI put trust in You; so, (please) keep me under Your supervision!\nوَاَسْتَنْصِرُكَ عَلَىٰ عَدُوِّيْ فَانْصُرْنِيْ\nWA ASTANSIRUKA A'LAA A'DUWWEE FANSURNEE\nI call for Your aid against my enemy; so, (please) grant me support!\nوَاَسْتَعِينُ بِكَ فَاَعِنِّيْ\nWA ASTA'EENU BIKA FA-A'INNEE\nI seek Your assistance; so, (please) assist me!\nوَاَسْتَغْفِرُكَ يَا اِلٰهِي فَاغْفِرْ لِيْ\nWA ASTAGHFIRUKA YAA ILAAHEE FAGHFIR LEE\nI ask for Your forgiveness; so, (please) forgive me.\nاٰمِيْنَ اٰمِيْنَ اٰمِيْنَ.\nAAMEENA AAMEENA AAMEEN\nSo, respond! Respond! Respond!",
    "Dua Ya Shahida Kulli Najwa\nEighth: It is also recommended to say the following supplication, which is also recommended on the night of Arafah. Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.), narrating from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.), said that Almighty Allah will forgive one who says this prayer on the night of Arafah or on Friday nights.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ يَا شَاهِدَ كُلِّ نَجْوَىٰ\nALLAAHUMMA YAA SHAAHIDA KULLI NAJWAA\nO Allah Who witnesses all secrets of hearts,\nوَمَوْضِعَ كُلِّ شَكْوَىٰ\nWA MAWDI'A KULLI SHAKWAA\nWho is the object of all complaints,\nوَعَالِمَ كُلِّ خَفِيَّةٍ\nWA A'ALIMA KULLI KHAFIYYAH\nWho knows all hidden things,\nوَمُنْتَهَىٰ كُلِّ حَاجَةٍ\nWA MUNTAHAA KULLI HAAJAH\nand Who is the aim of all needs!\nيَا مُبْتَدِئاً بِالنِّعَمِ عَلَىٰ الْعِبَادِ\nYAA MUBTADI'AN BIN NI'AMI A'LAL I'BAAD\nO He Who instigates favoring on the Servants!\nيَا كَرِيْمَ الْعَفْوِ\nYAA KAREEMAL A'FW\nO He Who is All-generous in pardoning!\nيَا حَسَنَ التَّجَاوُزِ\nYAA HASANAT TAJAAWUZ\nO He Who is All-excellent in overlooking!\nيَا جَوَادُ\nYAA JAWAAD\nO All-magnanimous!\nيَا مَنْ لَا يُوَارِيْ مِنْهُ لَيْلٌ دَاجٍ\nYAA MAN LAA YUWAAREE MINHU LAYLUN DAAJ\nO He Who cannot be concealed by the covering darkness of night,\nوَلَا بَحْرٌ عَجَّاجٌ\nWA LAA BAHRUN A'JJAAJ\nthe roaring clamor of oceans,\nوَلَا سَمَاءٌ ذَاتُ اَبْرَاجٍ\nWA LAA SAMAA'UN DHAATU ABRAAJ\nthe skies along with their constellations,\nوَلَا ظُلَمٌ ذَاتُ ارْتِتَاجٍ\nWA LAA ZULAMUN DHAATUR TITAAJ\nor the thunderous murk.\nيَا مَنِ الظُّلْمَةُ عِنْدَهٗ ضِيَاءٌ\nYAA MANIZ ZULMATU I'NDAHOO DIYAA'\nO He with Whom the entire murk is light,\nاَسْاَلُكَ بِنُوْرِ وَجْهِكَ الْكَرِيمِ\nAS'ALUKA BINOORI WAJHIKAL KAREEM\nI beseech You in the name of the brightness of Your Noble Face\nالَّذِي تَجَلَّيْتَ بِهٖ لِلْجَبَلِ فَجَعَلْتَهٗ دَكّاً\nALLADHEE TAJALLAYTA BIHEE LIL JABALI FAJA'ALTAHOO DAKKAA\nthrough which You manifested Your glory to the mountain; so, You made it crumble\nوَخَرَّ مُوسَىٰ صَعِقاً\nWA KHARRA MOOSAA SA'IQAA\nand (Prophet) Moses fell down in a swoon,\nوَبِاسْمِكَ الَّذِي رَفَعْتَ بِهٖ السَّمَاوَاتِ بِلَا عَمَدٍ\nWA BISMIKAL LADHEE RAFA'TA BIHIS SAMAAWAATI BILAA A'MAD\nin the name of Your Name by which You raised the heavens without any pillars\nوَسَطَحْتَ بِهٖ الْاَرْضَ عَلَىٰ وَجْهِ مَاءٍ جَمَدٍ\nWA SATAHTA BIHIL ARDA A'LAA WAJHI MAA'IN JAMAD\nand by which You flattened the earth on the surface of solid water,\nوَبِاسْمِكَ الْمَخْزُونِ الْمَكْنُونِ\nWA BISMIKAL MAKHZOONIL MAKNOON\nin the name of Your Name—the concealed, the stored,\nالْمَكْتُوبِ الطَّاهِرِ\nAL-MAKTOOBIT TAAHIR\nthe scribed, and the pure,\nالَّذِي اِذَا دُعِيْتَ، بِهٖ اَجَبْتَ\nALLADHEE IDHAA DU'EETA BIHEE AJABT\nwhich You answer any one who beseeches You in its name\nوَاِذَا سُئِلْتَ بِهٖ اَعْطَيْتَ\nWA IDHAA SU'ILTA BIHEE A'TAYT\nand grant any one who asks You his request,\nوَبِاسْمِكَ السُّبُّوحِ الْقُدُّوسِ الْبُرْهَانِ\nWA BISMIKAS SUBBOOHIL QUDDOOSIL BURHAAN\nin the name of Your Name; the Praised, Holy, and Demonstrative,\nالَّذِي هُوَ نُوْرٌ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ نُوْرٍ\nALLADHEE HUWA NOORUN A'LAA KULLI NOOR\nwhich is light over the entire light,\nوَنُورٌ مِنْ نُوْرٍ\nWA NOORUN MIN NOOR\nwhich is light made of light,\nيُضِيْۤءُ مِنْهُ كُلُّ نُوْرٍ\nYUDEE'U MINHU KULLU NOOR\nand from which all lights take their brightness;\nاِذَا بَلَغَ الْاَرْضَ انْشَقَّتْ\nIDHAA BALAGHAL ARDAN SHAQQAT\nif it reaches the earth, it will be rent asunder,\nوَاِذَا بَلَغَ السَّمَاوَاتِ فُتِحَتْ\nWA IDHAA BALAGHAS SAMAAWAATI FUTIHAT\nif it reaches the heavens, they will be opened,\nوَاِذَا بَلَغَ الْعَرْشَ اهْتَزَّ\nWA IDHAA BALAGHAL A'RSHAH TAZZ\nand if it reaches the throne, it will quiver;\nوَبِاسْمِكَ الَّذِي تَرْتَعِدُ مِنْهُ فَرَائِصُ مَلَاۤئِكَتِكَ\nWA BISMIKAL LADHEE TARTA'IDU MINHU FARAA'ISU MALAA'IKATIK\nand in the name of Your Name from the fear of which the muscles of Your angels tremble.\nوَاَسْاَلُكَ بِحَقِّ جَبْرَائِيلَ وَمِيكَائِيلَ وَاِسْرَافِيلَ\nWA AS'ALUKA BIHAQQI JABRAA'EELA WA MEEKAA'EELA WA ISRAAFEEL\nI beseech You in the name of [Archangels] Gabriel, Michael, and Seraph,\nوَبِحَقِّ مُحَمَّدٍ الْمُصْطَفَىٰ\nWA BIHAQQI MUHAMMADINIL MUSTAFAA\nin the name of Muhammad, the Divinely-chosen Prophet,\nصَلَّىٰ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَآلِهٖ\nSALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\npeace be upon him, his Household,\nوَعَلَىٰ جَمِيْعِ الْاَنْبِيَاءِ وَجَمِيعِ الْمَلَائِكَةِ\nWA A'LAA JAMEE'IL ANBIYAA'I WA JAMEE'IL MALAA'IKAH\nand all prophets and angels;\nوَبِالْاِسْمِ الَّذِي مَشَىٰ بِهٖ الْخِضْرُ عَلَىٰ قُلَلِ الْمَاءِ\nWA BIL ISMIL LADHEE MASHAA BIHIL KHIDRU A'LAA QULALIL MAA'\nin the name of the Name through which al-Khadir could walk on waters\nكَمَا مَشَىٰ بِهٖ عَلَىٰ جَدَدِ الْاَرْضِ\nKAMAA MASHAA BIHEE A'LAA JADADIL ARD\njust as he used to walk on lands;\nوَبِاسْمِكَ الَّذِي فَلَقْتَ بِهٖ الْبَحْرَ لِمُوسَىٰ\nWA BISMIKAL LADHEE FALAQTA BIHIL BAHRA LIMOOSAA\nin the name of You Name through which You caused the sea to cleave asunder for Moses,\nوَاَغْرَقْتَ فِرْعَوْنَ وَقَوْمَهٗ\nWA AGHRAQTA FIR'AWNA WA QAWMAH\nYou drowned Pharaoh and his people,\nوَاَنْجَيْتَ بِهٖ مُوسَىٰ بْنَ عِمْرَانَ وَمَنْ مَعَهٗ\nWA ANJAYTA BIHEE MOOSABNA I'MRAANA WA MAN MA'AH\nand saved Moses, the son of 'Imran, and those who accompanied him;\nوَبِاسْمِكَ الَّذِي دَعَاكَ بِهٖ مُوسَىٰ بْنُ عِمْرَانَ\nWA BISMIKAL LADHEE DA'AAKA BIHEE MOOSABNU I'MRAAN\nin the name of Your Name by which Moses, the son of 'Imran, besought You\nمِنْ جَانِبِ الطُّورِ الْاَيْمَنِ\nMIN JAANIBIT TOORIL AYMAN\nfrom the right slope of the Mount;\nفَاسْتَجَبْتَ لَهٗ وَالْقَيْتَ عَلَيْهِ مَحَبَّةً مِنْكَ\nFASTAJABTA LAHOO WAL QAYTA A'LAYHI MAHABBATAN MINK\nso, You responded to him and cast down upon him love from You;\nوَبِاسْمِكَ الَّذِي بِهٖ اَحْيَا عِيسَىٰ بْنُ مَرْيَمَ الْمَوْتَىٰ\nWA BISMIKAL LADHEE BIHEE AHYAA I'EESABNU MARYAMAL MAWTAA\nin the name of Your Name by which Jesus, the son of Mary, brought life to the dead,\nوَتَكَلَّمَ فِيْ الْمَهْدِ صَبِيّاً\nWA TAKALLAMA FIL MAHDI SABIYYAA\ncould speak while he was a child in the cradle,\nوَاَبْرَاُ الْاَكْمَهَ وَالْاَبْرَصَ بِاِذْنِكَ\nWA ABRA'UL AKMAHA WAL ABRASA BI-IDHNIK\nand healed the blind and the leprous by Your permission;\nوَبِاسْمِكَ الَّذِي دَعَاكَ بِهٖ حَمَلَةُ عَرْشِكَ\nWA BISMIKAL LADHEE DA'AAKA BIHEE HAMALATU A'RSHIK\nin the name of Your Name by which the bearers of Your Throne besought You\nوَجَبْرَائِيلُ وَمِيكَائِيلُ وَاِسْرَافِيلُ\nWA JABRAA'EELU WA MEEKAA'EELU WA ISRAAFEEL\nand so did Gabriel, Michael, Seraph,\nوَحَبِيبُكَ مُحَمَّدٌ صَلَّىٰ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَآلِهٖ\nWA HABEEBUKA MUHAMMADUN SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nMuhammad Your most beloved one (peace be upon him and upon his Household)\nوَمَلائِكَتُكَ الْمُقَرَّبُونَ\nWA MALAA'IKATUKAL MUQARRABOON\nYour favorite angels,\nوَاَنْبِيَاؤُكَ الْمُرْسَلُونَ\nWA ANBIYAA'UKAL MURSALOON\nYour messaged Prophets,\nوَعِبَادُكَ الصَّالِحُونَ مِنْ اَهْلِ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْاَرَضِينَ\nWA I'BAADUKAS SAALIHOONA MIN AHLIS SAMAAWAATI WAL ARADEEN\nand Your righteous servants from among the inhabitants of the heavens and the layers of the earth;\nوَبِاسْمِكَ الَّذِي دَعَاكَ بِهٖ ذُوْ النُّونِ\nWA BISMIKAL LADHEE DA'AAKA BIHEE DHUN NOON\nin the name of Your Name by which Dhu’l-Nun (Prophet Jonah) besought You\nاِذْ ذَهَبَ مُغَاضِباً فَظَنَّ اَنْ لَنْ تَقْدِرَ عَلَيْهِ\nIDH DHAHABA MUGHAADIBAN FAZANNA AN LAN TAQDIRA A'LAYH\nwhen he departed in wrath: he imagined that You had no power over him,\nفَنَادَىٰ فِي الظُّلُمَاتِ اَنْ لَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ سُبْحَانَكَ\nFANAADAA FIZ ZULUMAATI AN LAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANTA SUBHAANAK\nbut he cried through the depths of darkness, “There is no god but You. Glory be to You.\nاِنِّيْۤ كُنْتُ مِنَ الظَّالِمِينَ\nINNEE KUNTU MINAZ ZAALIMEEN\nI was indeed one of those who are wrong!”\nفَاسْتَجَبْتَ لَهٗ وَنَجَّيْتَهٗ مِنَ الْغَمِّ\nFASTAJABTA LAHOO WA NAJJAYTAHOO MINAL GHAMM\nSo, You responded to him and delivered him from the grief\nوَكَذٰلِكَ تُنْجِيْ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ\nWA KADHAALIKA TUNJIL MU'MINEEN\nand thus do You deliver the believers;\nوَبِاسْمِكَ الْعَظِيمِ الَّذِي دَعَاكَ بِهٖ دَاوُودُ\nWA BISMIKAL A'ZEEMIL LADHEE DA'AAKA BIHEE DAAWOOD\nin the name of Your Great Name by which David besought You\nوَخَرَّ لَكَ سَاجِداً فَغَفَرْتَ لَهٗ ذَنْبَهٗ\nWA KHARRA LAKA SAAJIDAN FAGHAFARTA LAHOO DHANBAH\nand as he fell down prostrating himself to You, You rectified it for him;\nوَبِاسْمِكَ الَّذِي دَعَتْكَ بِهٖ اٰسِيَةُ امْرَاَةُ فِرْعَوْنَ\nWA BISMIKAL LADHEE DA'ATKA BIHEE AASIYATUM RA'ATU FIR'AWN\nin the name of Your Name by which Asiyah, the wife of Pharaoh, besought You,\nاِذْ قَالَتْ: ”رَبِّ ابْنِ لِيْ عِنْدَكَ بَيْتاً فِي الْجَنَّةِ\nIDH QAALAT RABBIBNI LEE I'NDAKA BAYTAN FIL JANNAH\nsaying, “My Lord! Build for me a house with You in Paradise,\nوَنَجِّنِي مِنْ فِرْعَوْنَ وَعَمَلِهٖ\nWA NAJJINEE MIN FIR'AWNA WA A'MALIH\ndeliver me from Pharaoh and his doing,\nوَنَجِّنِي مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الظَّالِمِينَ“\nWA NAJJINEE MINAL QAWMIZ ZAALIMEEN\nand deliver me from the unjust people.”\nفَاسْتَجَبْتَ لَهَا دُعَاءَهَا\nFASTAJABTA LAHAA DU'AA'AHAA\nSo, You responded to her prayer;\nوَبِاسْمِكَ الَّذِي دَعَاكَ بِهٖ اَيُّوْبُ اِذْ حَلَّ بِهٖ الْبَلَاءُ\nWA BISMIKAL LADHEE DA'AAKA BIHEE AYYOOBU IDH HALLA BIHIL BALAA'\nin the name of Your Name by which (Prophet) Job besought You after misfortune had befallen him;\nفَعَافَيْتَهٗ وَآتَيْتَهٗ اَهْلَهٗ وَمِثْلَهُمْ مَعَهُمْ\nFA'AAFAYTAHOO WA AATAYTAHOO AHLAHOO WA MITHLAHUM MA'AHUM\nso, You healed him and gave him his family and the like of them with them:\nرَحْمَةً مِنْ عِنْدِكَ وَذِكْرَىٰ لِلْعَابِدِيْنَ\nRAHMATAN MIN I'NDIKA WA DHIKRAA LIL A'ABIDEEN\na mercy from You and a reminder to the worshippers;\nوَبِاسْمِكَ الَّذِي دَعَاكَ بِهٖ يَعْقُوْبُ\nWA BISMIKAL LADHEE DA'AAKA BIHEE YA'QOOB\nin the name of Your Name by which (Prophet) Jacob besought You;\nفَرَدَدْتَ عَلَيْهِ بَصَرَهٗ وَقُرَّةَ عَيْنِهٖ يُوْسُفَ وَجَمَعْتَ شَمْلَهٗ\nFARADADTA A'LAYHI BASARAHOO WA QURRATA A'YNIHEE YOOSUFA WA JAMA'TA SHAMLAH\nso, You returned to him his sight and the delight of his heart, Joseph, and You reunified him.\nوَبِاسْمِكَ الَّذِي دَعَاكَ بِهٖ سُلَيْمَانُ\nWA BISMIKAL LADHEE DA'AAKA BIHEE SULAYMAAN\nin the name of Your Name by which (Prophet) Solomon besought You;\nفَوَهَبْتَ لَهٗ مُلْكاً لَا يَنْبَغِيْ لِاَحَدٍ مِنْ بَعْدِهٖ\nFAWAHABTA LAHOO MULKAN LAA YANBAGHEE LI-AHADIN MIN BA'DIH\nSo, You gifted him kingdom that none else should never gain,\nاِنَّكَ اَنْتَ الْوَهَّابُ\nINNAKA ANTAL WAHHAAB\nfor You are verily the Granter of bounties;\nوَبِاسْمِكَ الَّذِي سَخَّرْتَ بِهٖ الْبُرَاقَ لِمُحَمَّدٍ\nWA BISMIKAL LADHEE SAKHKHARTA BIHIL BURAAQA LIMUHAMMAD\nin the name of Your Name by which You subdued the Buraq to Muhammad,\nصَلَّىٰ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَآلِهٖ وَسَلَّمَ\nSALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIHEE WA SALLAM\npeace and blessings be upon him and his Household,\nاِذْ قَالَ تَعَالَىٰ: ”سُبْحَانَ الَّذِي اَسْرٰى بِعَبْدِهٖ لَيْلاً\nIDH QAALA TA'AALAA SUBHAANAL LADHEE ASRAA BI-A'BDIHEE LAYLAA\nas Almighty Allah says, “Glory be to Him Who made His servant to go on a night\nمِنَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ اِلَىٰ الْمَسْجِدِ الْاَقْصَىٰ“\nMINAL MASJIDIL HARAAMI ILAL MASJIDIL AQSAA\nfrom the Sacred Mosque to the remote mosque.”\nوَقَوْلُهٗ: ”سُبْحَانَ الَّذِي سَخَّرَ لَنَا هٰذَا وَمَا كُنَّا لَهٗ مُقْرِنِيْنَ\nWA QAWLUHOO SUBHAANAL LADHEE SAKHKHARA LANAA HAADHAA WA MAA KUNNAA LAHOO MUQRINEEN\nHe also says, “Glory be to Him Who made this subservient to us and we were not able to do it.\nوَاِنَّا اِلَىٰ رَبِّنَا لَمُنْقَلِبُوْنَ\nWA INNAA ILAA RABBINAA LAMUNQALIBOON\nSurely, to our Lord we must return;”\nوَبِاسْمِكَ الَّذِي تَنَزَّلَ بِهٖ جَبْرَائِيلُ عَلَىٰ مُحَمَّدٍ\nWA BISMIKAL LADHEE TANAZZALA BIHEE JABRAA'EELU A'LAA MUHAMMAD\nin the name of Your Name by which (Archangel) Gabriel used to ascend to Muhammad,\nصَلَّىٰ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَآلِهٖ\nSALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\npeace be upon him and his Household;\nوَبِاسْمِكَ الَّذِي دَعَاكَ بِهٖ اٰدَمُ\nWA BISMIKAL LADHEE DA'AAKA BIHEE AADAM\nand in the name of Your Name by which Adam besought You;\nفَغَفَرْتَ لَهٗ ذَنْبَهٗ وَاَسْكَنْتَهٗ جَنَّتَكَ\nFAGHAFARTA LAHOO DHANBAHOO WA ASKANTAHOO JANNATAK\nso, You rectified him and allowed him to dwell in Your Paradise.\nوَاَسْاَلُكَ بِحَقِّ الْقُرْآنِ الْعَظِيمِ\nWA AS'ALUKA BIHAQQIL QUR'AANIL A'ZEEM\nI beseech You in the name of the Great Qur'an,\nوَبِحَقِّ مُحَمَّدٍ خَاتَمِ النَّبِيِّينَ\nWA BIHAQQI MUHAMMADIN KHAATAMIN NABIYYEEN\nin the name of Muhammad, the Seal of the Prophets,\nوَبِحَقِّ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ\nWA BIHAQQI IBRAAHEEM\nin the name of Abraham,\nوَبِحَقِّ فَصْلِكَ يَوْمَ الْقَضَاءِ\nWA BIHAQQI FASLIKA YAWMAL QADAA'\nin the name of Your Judgment on the Day of the Administration of Justice,\nوَبِحَقِّ الْمَوَازِينِ اِذَا نُصِبَتْ\nWA BIHAQQIL MAWAAZEENI IDHAA NUSIBAT\nin the name of the Scales when they shall be set up,\nوَالصُّحُفِ اِذَا نُشِرَتْ\nWAS SUHUFI IDHAA NUSHIRAT\nthe Scrolls when they shall be laid open,\nوَبِحَقِّ الْقَلَمِ وَمَا جَرَىٰ\nWA BIHAQQIL QALAMI WA MAA JARAA\nthe Pen and whatever has been decided,\nوَاللَّوْحِ وَمَا اَحْصٰى\nWAL LAWHI WA MAA AHSAA\nand the Tablet and whatever it has recorded;\nوَبِحَقِّ الْاِسْمِ الَّذِي كَتَبْتَهٗ عَلَىٰ سُرَادِقِ الْعَرْشِ\nWA BIHAQQIL ISMIL LADHEE KATABTAHOO A'LAA SURAADIQIL A'RSH\nin the name of the Name that You had inscribed on the pavilion of the Divine Throne\nقَبْلَ خَلْقِكَ الْخَلْقَ وَالدُّنْيَا\nQABLA KHALQIKAL KHALQA WAD DUNYAA\ntwo thousand years before You created the beings, the world,\nوَالشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ بِاَلْفَيْ عَامٍ\nWASH SHAMSA WAL QAMARA BI-ALFAY A'AM\nthe sun, and the moon.\nوَاَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللَّهُ\nWA ASH-HADU AN LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAH\nI bear witness that there is no god save Allah,\nوَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ\nWAHDAHOO LAA SHAREEKA LAH\nalone without having any partner,\nوَاَنَّ مُحَمَّداً عَبْدُهٗ وَرَسُولُهٗ\nWA ANNA MUHAMMADAN A'BDUHOO WA RASOOLUH\nand that Muhammad is his servant and messenger.\nوَاَسْاَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ الْمَخْزُونِ فِيْ خَزَائِنِكَ\nWA AS'ALUKA BISMIKAL MAKHZOONI FEE KHAZAA'INIK\nI beseech You in the name of Your Name that is hoarded in Your stores,\nالَّذِي اسْتَاْثَرْتَ بِهٖ فِيْ عِلْمِ الْغَيْبِ عِنْدَكَ\nALLADHIS TA'THARTA BIHEE FEE I'LMIL GHAYBI I'NDAK\nYou have kept in the knowledge of the Unseen with You\nلَمْ يَظْهَرْ عَلَيْهِ اَحَدٌ مِنْ خَلْقِكَ\nLAM YAZHAR A'LAYHI AHADUN MIN KHALQIK\nand it has not been shown to any of Your creatures,\nلَا مَلَكٌ مُقَرَّبٌ\nLAA MALAKUN MUQARRAB\nbe him a favorite angel,\nوَلَا نَبِيٌّ مُرْسَلٌ\nWA LAA NABIYYUN MURSAL\na missioned Prophet,\nوَلَا عَبْدٌ مُصْطَفَىٰ\nWA LAA A'BDUN MUSTAFAA\nor a chosen servant.\nوَاَسْاَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِي شَقَقْتَ بِهٖ الْبِحَارَ\nWA AS'ALUKA BISMIKAL LADHEE SHAQAQTA BIHIL BIHAAR\nI beseech You in the name of Your Name by which You rent asunder the oceans,\nوَقَامَتْ بِهٖ الْجِبَالُ\nWA QAAMAT BIHIL JIBAAL\nthe mountains rose,\nوَاخْتَلَفَ بِهٖ اللَّيْلُ وَالنَّهَارُ\nWAKHTALAFA BIHIL LAYLU WAN NAHAAR\nand night and day follow each other,\nوَبِحَقِّ السَّبْعِ الْمَثَانِي وَالْقُرْآنِ الْعَظِيمِ\nWA BIHAQQIS SAB'IL MATHAANEE WAL QUR'AANIL A'ZEEM\nin the name of the seven of the oft-repeated verses and the Grand Qur'an,\nوَبِحَقِّ الْكِرَامِ الْكَاتِبِينَ\nWA BIHAQQIL KIRAAMIL KAATIBEEN\nin the name of the noble, recording angels,\nوَبِحَقِّ طٰهٰ وَيس وَكهيعص\nWA BIHAQQI TAA HAA WA YAA SEEN WA KAAAF HAA YAA A'YN SAAAD\nin the name of Ta-Ha, Ya-Sin, Kaf-Ha-Ya-'Ayn-Sad,\nوَحم عسق\nWA HAA MEEM A'YN SEEN QAAAF\nHa-Mim-'Ayn-Sin-Qaf,\nوَبِحَقِّ تَوْرَاةِ مُوسَىٰ\nWA BIHAQQI TAWRAATI MOOSAA\nand in the name of the Torah of Moses,\nوَاِنْجِيلِ عِيسَىٰ\nWA INJEELI I'EESAA\nthe Gospel of Jesus,\nوَزَبُورِ دَاوُودَ\nWA ZABOORI DAAWOOD\nthe Psalms of David,\nوَفُرْقَانِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nWA FURQAANI MUHAMMAD\nthe Furqan (Criterion) of Muhammad,\nصَلَّىٰ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَآلِهٖ\nSALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\npeace be upon him, his Household,\nوَعَلَىٰ جَمِيْعِ الرُّسُلِ وَبَاهِيّاً شَرَاهِيّاً\nWA A'LAA JAMEE'IR RUSULI WA BAAHIYYAN SHARAAHIYYAA\nand all the messengers and bahiyya sharahiyya.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْۤ اَسْاَلُكَ بِحَقِّ تِلْكَ الْمُنَاجَاةِ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUKA BIHAQQI TILKAL MUNAAJAAH\nO Allah, I beseech You in the name of this confidential talk\nالَّتِي كَانَتْ بَيْنَكَ وَبَيْنَ مُوسَىٰ بْنِ عِمْرَانَ\nALLATEE KAANAT BAYNAKA WA BAYNA MOOSABNI I'MRAAN\nwhich took place between You and Moses, the son of 'Imran,\nفَوْقَ جَبَلِ طُوْرِ سَيْنَاءَ\nFAWQA JABALI TOORI SAYNAA'\non the Mount Tur Sayna',\nوَاَسْاَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِي عَلَّمْتَهٗ مَلَكَ الْمَوْتِ لِقَبْضِ الْاَرْوَاحِ\nWA AS'ALUKA BISMIKAL LADHEE A'LLAMTAHOO MALAKAL MAWTI LIQABDIL ARWAAH\nI beseech You in the name of Your Name which You taught the Angel of Death so that he would be able to grasp the souls,\nوَاَسْاَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِي كُتِبَ عَلَىٰ وَرَقِ الزَّيْتُونِ\nWA AS'ALUKA BISMIKAL LADHEE KUTIBA A'LAA WARAQIZ ZAYTOON\nI beseech You in the name of Your Name which was written on the leaves of olive-trees;\nفَخَضَعَتِ النِّيرَانُ لِتِلْكَ الْوَرَقَةِ\nFAKHADA'ATIN NEERAANU LITILKAL WARAQAH\nso, fires subdued to these leaves\nفَقُلْتَ: ”يَا نَارُ كُوْنِيْ بَرْداً وَسَلَاماً“\nFAQULTA YAA NAARU KOONEE BARDAN WA SALAAMAA\nafter You said, “O fire! Be a comfort and peace,”\nوَاَسْاَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِي كَتَبْتَهٗ عَلَىٰ سُرَادِقِ الْمَجْدِ وَالْكَرَامَةِ\nWA AS'ALUKA BISMIKAL LADHEE KATABTAHOO A'LAA SURAADIQIL MAJDI WAL KARAAMAH\nand I beseech You in the name of Your Name that You wrote on the canopies of Glory and Dignity.\nيَا مَنْ لَا يُخْفِيهِ سَائِلٌ\nYAA MAN LAA YUKHFEEHI SAA'IL\nO He Who cannot be annoyed by any beseecher\nوَلَا يَنْقُصُهٗ نَائِلٌ\nWA LAA YANQUSUHOO NAA'IL\nHe Who cannot be influenced by any reward (that He presents)!\nيَا مَنْ بِهٖ يُسْتَغَاثُ وَاِلَيْهِ يُلْجَاُ\nYAA MAN BIHEE YUSTAGHAATHU WA ILAYHI YULJA'\nO He Whose refuge is taken and to Whom resort is made!\nاَسْاَلُكَ بِمَعَاقِدِ الْعِزِّ مِنْ عَرْشِكَ\nAS'ALUKA BIMA'AAQIDIL I'ZZI MIN A'RSHIK\nI beseech You in the name of the Seats of Honor belonging to Your Throne,\nوَمُنْتَهَىٰ الرَّحْمَةِ مِنْ كِتَابِكَ\nWA MUNTAHAR RAHMATI MIN KITAABIK\nthe utmost of mercy in Your Book,\nوَبِاسْمِكَ الْاَعْظَمِ\nWA BISMIKAL A'ZAM\nYour All-great Name,\nوَجَدِّكَ الْاَعْلَىٰ\nWA JADDIKAL A'LAA\nYour All-high majesty,\nوَكَلِمَاتِكَ التَّامَّاتِ الْعُلَىٰ\nWA KALIMAATIKAT TAAMMAATIL U'LAA\nand Your most high, perfect Words.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ رَبَّ الرِّيَاحِ وَمَا ذَرَتْ\nALLAAHUMMA RABBAR RIYAAHI WA MAA DHARAT\nO Allah, Lord of winds and whatever they scatter far,\nوَالسَّمَاءِ وَمَا اَظَلَّتْ\nWAS SAMAA'I WA MAA AZALLAT\nLord of the sky and whatever it covers,\nوَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا اَقَلَّتْ\nWAL ARDI WA MAA AQALLAT\nthe Lord of the earth and whatever it carries,\nوَالشَّيَاطِينِ وَمَا اَضَلَّتْ\nWASH SHAYAATEENI WA MAA ADALLAT\nthe Lord of the devils and whomever they mislead,\nوَالْبِحَارِ وَمَا جَرَتْ\nWAL BIHAARI WA MAA JARAT\nand the Lord of the oceans and wherever they flow.\nوَبِحَقِّ كُلِّ حَقٍّ هُوَ عَلَيْكَ حَقٌّ\nWA BIHAQQI KULLI HAQQIN HUWA A'LAYKA HAQQ\nI beseech You in the name of everything that enjoys a right with You,\nوَبِحَقِّ الْمَلَائِكَةِ الْمُقَرَّبِينَ\nWA BIHAQQIL MALAA'IKATIL MUQARRABEEN\nin the name of the favorite angels,\nوَالرَّوْحَانِيِّينَ وَالْكَرُّوبِيِّينَ\nWAR RAWHAANIYYEENA WAL KARROOBIYYEEN\nthe angels managing the spirits, the cherubim,\nوَالْمُسَبِّحِينَ لَكَ بِاللَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ لَا يَفْتُرُوْنَ\nWAL MUSABBIHEENA LAKA BIL LAYLI WAN NAHAARI LAA YAFTUROON\nand the angels praising You night and day without showing sluggishness,\nوَبِحَقِّ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ خَلِيْلِكَ\nWA BIHAQQI IBRAAHEEMA KHALEELIK\nin the name of Abraham, Your intimate friend,\nوَبِحَقِّ كُلِّ وَلِيٍّ يُنَادِيْكَ بَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالْمَرْوَةِ\nWA BIHAQQI KULLI WALIYYIN YUNAADEEKA BAYNAS SAFAA WAL MARWAH\nand in the name of each and every saint who calls You between Safa and Marwah\nوَتَسْتَجِيبُ لَهٗ دُعَاءَهٗ\nWA TASTAJEEBU LAHOO DU'AA'AH\nand You respond to his/her prayer.\nيَا مُجِيْبُ اَسْاَلُكَ بِحَقِّ هٰذِهِ الْاَسْمَاءِ وَبِهٰذِهِ الدَّعَوَاتِ\nYAA MUJEEBU AS'ALUKA BIHAQQI HAADHIHIL ASMAA'I WA BIHAADHIHID DA'AWAAT\nO Responsive Lord! I beseech You in the name of all these names and all these prayers\nاَنْ تَغْفِرَ لَنَا مَا قَدَّمْنَا وَمَا اَخَّرْنَا\nAN TAGHFIRA LANAA MAA QADDAMNAA WA MAA AKHKHARNAA\nto forgive us all our past and coming sins,\nوَمَا اَسْرَرْنَا وَمَا اَعْلَنَّا\nWA MAA ASRARNAA WA MAA A'LANNAA\nincluding the secret and the open,\nوَمَا اَبْدَيْنَا وَمَا اَخْفَيْنَا\nWA MAA ABDAYNAA WA MAA AKHFAYNAA\nthe hidden and the public,\nوَمَا اَنْتَ اَعْلَمُ بِهٖ مِنَّا\nWA MAA ANTA A'LAMU BIHEE MINNAA\nand those whom You know better than we do.\nاِنَّكَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ\nINNAKA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEER\nVerily, You have power over all things.\nبِرَحْمَتِكَ يَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِينَ\nBIRAHMATIKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\n[Respond] in the name of Your mercy, O most Merciful of all those who show mercy.\nيَا حَافِظَ كُلِّ غَرِيْبٍ\nYAA HAAFIZA KULLI GHAREEB\nO He Who guards all strangers!\nيَا مُؤْنِسَ كُلِّ وَحِيْدٍ\nYAA MU'NISA KULLI WAHEED\nO He Who brings entertainment to all lonely ones!\nيَا قُوَّةَ كُلِّ ضَعِيْفٍ\nYAA QUWWATA KULLI DA'EEF\nO He Who is the power of all the weak!\nيَا نَاصِرَ كُلِّ مَظْلُوْمٍ\nYAA NAASIRA KULLI MAZLOOM\nO He Who is the support of all the persecuted!\nيَا رَازِقَ كُلِّ مَحْرُوْمٍ\nYAA RAAZIQA KULLI MAHROOM\nO He Who bestows upon all the deprived!\nيَا مُؤْنِسَ كُلِّ مُسْتَوْحِشٍ\nYAA MU'NISA KULLI MUSTAWHISH\nO He Who brings entertainment to all the lonesome!\nيَا صَاحِبَ كُلِّ مُسَافِرٍ\nYAA SAAHIBA KULLI MUSAAFIR\nO He Who is the company of all those on journeys!\nيَا عِمَادَ كُلِّ حَاضِرٍ\nYAA I'MAADA KULLI HAADIR\nO He Who is the pillar of all the present!\nيَا غَافِرَ كُلِّ ذَنْبٍ وَخَطِيئَةٍ\nYAA GHAAFIRA KULLI DHANBIN WA KHATEE'AH\nO He Who forgives all sins and offenses!\nيَا غِيَاثَ الْمُسْتَغِيثِينَ\nYAA GHIYAATHAL MUSTAGHEETHEEN\nO He Who is the aid of all those begging aid!\nيَا صَرِيْخَ الْمُسْتَصْرِخِينَ\nYAA SAREEKHAL MUSTASRIKHEEN\nO He Who is the relief of all those pleading for relief!\nيَا كَاشِفَ كَرْبِ الْمَكْرُوبِينَ\nYAA KAASHIFA KARBIL MAKROOBEEN\nO He Who relieves the calamity of those inflicted with calamities!\nيَا فَارِجَ هَمِّ الْمَهْمُومِينَ\nYAA FAARIJA HAMMIL MAHMOOMEEN\nO He Who alleviate the distress of the distressed ones!\nيَا بَدِيْعَ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْاَرَضِينَ\nYAA BADEE'AS SAMAAWAATI WAL ARADEEN\nO He Who is the Originator of the heavens and the layers of the earth!\nيَا مُنْتَهَىٰ غَايَةِ الطَّالِبِينَ\nYAA MUNTAHAA GHAAYATIT TAALIBEEN\nO He Who is the utmost hope of the seekers!\nيَا مُجِيْبَ دَعْوَةِ الْمُضْطَرِّينَ\nYAA MUJEEBA DA'WATIL MUDTARREEN\nO He Who responds to the prayers of the troubled!\nيَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِينَ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nO He Who is the most Merciful of all those who show mercy!\nيَا رَبَّ الْعَالَمِينَ\nYAA RABBAL A'ALAMEEN\nO Lord of the worlds!\nيَا دَيَّانَ يَوْمِ الدِّينِ\nYAA DAYYAANA YAWMID DEEN\nO Master of the Judgment Day!\nيَا اَجْوَدَ الْاَجْوَدِينَ\nYAA AJWADAL AJWADEEN\nO most Magnanimous of all those who act magnanimously!\nيَا اَكْرَمَ الْاَكْرَمِينَ\nYAA AKRAMAL AKRAMEEN\nO most Generous of all those who act generously!\nيَا اَسْمَعَ السَّامِعِينَ\nYAA ASMA'AS SAAMI'EEN\nO most Hearing of all those who can hear!\nيَا اَبْصَرَ النَّاظِرِينَ\nYAA ABSARAN NAAZIREEN\nO most Seeing of all those who can see!\nيَا اَقْدَرَ الْقَادِرِينَ\nYAA AQDARAL QAADIREEN\nO most Powerful of all those who have power!\nاغْفِرْ لِيَ الذُّنُوبَ الَّتِي تُغَيِّرُ النِّعَمَ\nIGHFIR LIYADH DHUNOOBAL LATEE TUGHAYYIRUN NI'AM\n(Please) forgive my sins that change the bounties\nوَاغْفِرْ لِيَ الذُّنُوبَ الَّتِي تُوْرِثُ النَّدَمَ\nWAGHFIR LIYADH DHUNOOBAL LATEE TOORITHUN NADAM\nAnd forgive me my sins that bring about remorse,\nوَاغْفِرْ لِيَ الذُّنُوبَ الَّتِي تُوْرِثُ السَّقَمَ\nWAGHFIR LIYADH DHUNOOBAL LATEE TOORITHUS SAQAM\nforgive me my sins that result in ailment,\nوَاغْفِرْ لِيَ الذُّنُوبَ الَّتِي تَهْتِكُ الْعِصَمَ\nWAGHFIR LIYADH DHUNOOBAL LATEE TAHTIKUL I'SAM\nforgive me my sins that tear safeguards,\nوَاغْفِرْ لِيَ الذُّنُوبَ الَّتِي تَرُدُّ الدُّعَاءَ\nWAGHFIR LIYADH DHUNOOBAL LATEE TARUDDUD DU'AA'\nforgive me my sins that repel prayers,\nوَاغْفِرْ لِيَ الذُّنُوبَ الَّتِي تَحْبِسُ قَطْرَ السَّمَاءِ\nWAGHFIR LIYADH DHUNOOBAL LATEE TAHBISU QATRAS SAMAA'\nforgive me my sins that withhold the drops of the sky,\nوَاغْفِرْ لِيَ الذُّنُوبَ الَّتِي تُعَجِّلُ الْفَنَاءَ\nWAGHFIR LIYADH DHUNOOBAL LATEE TU'AJJILUL FANAA'\nforgive me my sins that hasten extinction,\nوَاغْفِرْ لِيَ الذُّنُوبَ الَّتِي تَجْلِبُ الشَّقَاءَ\nWAGHFIR LIYADH DHUNOOBAL LATEE TAJLIBUSH SHAQAA'\nforgive me my sins that beget misery,\nوَاغْفِرْ لِيَ الذُّنُوبَ الَّتِي تُظْلِمُ الْهَوَاءَ\nWAGHFIR LIYADH DHUNOOBAL LATEE TUZLIMUL HAWAA'\nforgive me my sins that darken the atmospheres,\nوَاغْفِرْ لِيَ الذُّنُوبَ الَّتِي تَكْشِفُ الْغِطَاءَ\nWAGHFIR LIYADH DHUNOOBAL LATEE TAKSHIFUL GHITAA'\nforgive me my sins that disclose the coverings,\nوَاغْفِرْ لِيَ الذُّنُوبَ الَّتِي لَا يَغْفِرُهَا غَيْرُكَ يَا اَللّٰهُ\nWAGHFIR LIYADH DHUNOOBAL LATEE LAA YAGHFIRUHAA GHAYRUKA YAA ALLAAH\nforgive me my sins that none can forgive save You, O Allah,\nوَاحْمِلْ عَنِّيْ كُلَّ تَبِعَةٍ لِاَحَدٍ مِنْ خَلْقِكَ\nWAHMIL A'NNEE KULLA TABI'ATIN LI-AHADIN MIN KHALQIK\nbear from me every offensive that I have made against any of Your creatures,\nوَاجْعَلْ لِيْ مِنْ اَمْرِيْ فَرَجاً وَمَخْرَجاً وَيُسْراً\nWAJ'AL LEE MIN AMREE FARAJAN WA MAKHRAJAN WA YUSRAA\nmake all my affairs reach at relief, exit, and easiness,\nوَاَنْزِلْ يَقِيْنَكَ فِيْ صَدْرِيْ\nWA ANZIL YAQEENAKA FEE SADREE\nmake Your tranquility ascend on my chest,\nوَرَجَاءَكَ فِيْ قَلْبِيْ حَتَّىٰ لَا اَرْجُوَ غَيْرَكَ\nWA RAJAA'AKA FEE QALBEE HATTAA LAA ARJUWA GHAYRAK\nand make hope in You ascend on my heart so that I shall never hope for anyone save You.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ احْفَظْنِيْ وَعَافِنِي فِيْ مَقَامِيْ\nALLAAHUMMAH FAZNEE WA A'AFINEE FEE MAQAAMEE\nO Allah, (please) safeguard me, heal me in all my situations,\nوَاصْحَبْنِي فِيْ لَيْلِيْ وَنَهَارِي\nWAS-HABNEE FEE LAYLEE WA NAHAAREE\nbe my companion at nights and days,\nوَمِنْ بَيْنِ يَدَيَّ وَمِنْ خَلْفِيْ\nWA MIN BAYNI YADAYYA WA MIN KHALFEE\nbe ahead of me, behind me,\nوَعَنْ يَمِيْنِيْ وَعَنْ شِمَالِيْ\nWA A'N YAMEENEE WA A'N SHIMAALEE\nfrom my right side, from my left side,\nوَمِنْ فَوْقِيْ وَمِنْ تَحْتِيْ\nWA MIN FAWQEE WA MIN TAHTEE\nfrom above me, and from beneath me,\nوَيَسِّرْ لِيَ السَّبِيلَ\nWA YASSIR LIYAS SABEEL\nmake easy all the ways for me,\nوَاَحْسِنْ لِيَ التَّيْسِيرَ\nWA AHSIN LIYAT TAYSEER\nmake excellent facilitation for me,\nوَلَا تَخْذُلْنِيْ فِي الْعَسِيرِ\nWA LAA TAKHDHULNEE FIL A'SEER\ndo not disappoint me in hardships,\nوَاهْدِنِي يَا خَيْرَ دَلِيْلٍ،\nWAHDINEE YAA KHAYRA DALEEL\nguide me, O Best of all guides,\nوَلَا تَكِلْنِيْ اِلَى نَفْسِيْ فِيْ الْاُمُورِ\nWA LAA TAKILNEE ILAA NAFSEE FIL UMOOR\ndo not leave me alone in all my affairs,\nوَلَقِّنِي كُلَّ سُرُوْرٍ\nWA LAQQINEE KULLA SUROOR\nmake me receive all pleasures,\nوَاقْلِبْنِي اِلَىٰ اَهْلِيْ بِالْفَلَاحِ وَالنَّجَاحِ\nWAQLIBNEE ILAA AHLEE BIL FALAAHI WAN NAJAAH\nand make me return to my family with prosperity, success,\nمَحْبُوْرًا فِي الْعَاجِلِ وَالْاٰجِلِ\nMAHBOORAN FIL A'AJILI WAL AAJIL\nand gladness in the present and in the future.\nاِنَّكَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ\nINNAKA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEER\nVerily, You have power over all things.\nوَارْزُقْنِي مِنْ فَضْلِكَ\nWARZUQNEE MIN FADLIK\n(Please) bestow upon me with Your favors,\nوَاَوْسِعْ عَلَيَّ مِنْ طَيِّبَاتِ رِزْقِكَ\nWA AWSI' A'LAYYA MIN TAYYIBAATI RIZQIK\nexpand for me the most favorable of Your sustenance,\nوَاسْتَعْمِلْنِي فِيْ طَاعَتِكَ\nWASTA'MILNEE FEE TAA'ATIK\napply me to the obedience to You,\nوَاَجِرْنِي مِنْ عَذَابِكَ وَنَارِكَ\nWA AJIRNEE MIN A'DHAABIKA WA NAARIK\nredeem me from Your chastisement and Fire,\nوَاقْلِبْنِي اِذَا تَوَفَّيْتَنِيْۤ اِلَىٰ جَنَّتِكَ بِرَحْمَتِكَ\nWAQLIBNEE IDHAA TAWAFFAYTANEE ILAA JANNATIKA BIRAHMATIK\nand when You grasp my soul, lead me to Your Paradise, by Your mercy.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّي اَعُوْذُ بِكَ مِنْ زَوَالِ نِعْمَتِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE A'OODHU BIKA MIN ZAWAALI NI'MATIK\nO Allah, I seek Your protection against confiscation of Your graces,\nوَمِنْ تَحْوِيْلِ عَافِيَتِكَ\nWA MIN TAHWEELI A'AFIYATIK\nagainst alternation of Your conferral of wellbeing on me,\nوَمِنْ حُلُوْلِ نَقِمَتِكَ\nWA MIN HULOOLI NAQIMATIK\nagainst the befalling of Your punishment,\nوَمِنْ نُزُوْلِ عَذَابِكَ\nWA MIN NUZOOLI A'DHAABIK\nand against the ensuing of Your chastisement.\nوَاَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنْ جَهْدِ الْبَلَاءِ\nWA A'OODHU BIKA MIN JAHDIL BALAA'\nI seek Your protection against arduous hardships,\nوَدَرَكِ الشَّقَاءِ\nWA DARAKISH SHAQAA'\nagainst coming about of misery,\nوَمِنْ سُوْۤءِ الْقَضَاءِ\nWA MIN SOO'IL QADAA'\nagainst evil end results,\nوَشَمَاتَةِ الْاَعْدَاءِ\nWA SHAMAATATIL A'DAA'\nagainst my enemies’ gloating over my grief,\nوَمِنْ شَرِّ مَا يَنْزِلُ مِنَ السَّمَاءِ\nWA MIN SHARRI MAA YANZILU MINAS SAMAA'\nagainst the evil of everything that ascends from the heavens,\nوَمِنْ شَرِّ مَا فِيْ الْكِتَابِ الْمُنْزَلِ\nWA MIN SHARRI MAA FIL KITAABIL MUNZAL\nand against the evils mentioned in the Revealed Book.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ لَا تَجْعَلْنِيْ مِنَ الْاَشْرَارِ\nALLAAHUMMA LAA TAJ'ALNEE MINAL ASHRAAR\nO Allah, (please) do not include me with the evil ones,\nوَلَا مِنْ اَصْحَابِ النَّارِ\nWA LAA MIN AS-HAABIN NAAR\ndo not include me with the people of Hellfire,\nوَلَا تَحْرِمْنِيْ صُحْبَةَ الْاَخْيَارِ\nWA LAA TAHRIMNEE SUHBATAL AKHYAAR\ndo not deprive me of the companionship of the upright people,\nوَاَحْيِنِي حَيَاةً طَيِّبَةً\nWA AHYINEE HAYAATAN TAYYIBAH\ngrant me a pleasant lifetime,\nوَتَوَفَّنِي وَفَاةً طَيِّبَةً تُلْحِقُنِيْ بِالْاَبْرَارِ\nWA TAWAFFANEE WAFAATAN TAYYIBATAN TULHIQUNEE BIL ABRAAR\ndecide for me a kind of death due to which You will join me to the Pious Ones,\nوَارْزُقْنِي مُرَافَقَةَ الْاَنْبِيَاءِ\nWARZUQNEE MURAAFAQATAL ANBIYAA'\nand confer upon me with the companionship of the Prophets\nفِيْ مَقْعَدِ صِدْقٍ عِنْدَ مَلِيْكٍ مُقْتَدِرٍ\nFEE MAQ'ADI SIDQIN I'NDA MALEEKIN MUQTADIR\nin the seat of honesty with the All-powerful King.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ لَكَ الْحَمْدُ عَلَىٰ حُسْنِ بَلَائِكَ وَصُنْعِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA LAKAL HAMDU A'LAA HUSNI BALAA'IKA WA SUN'IK\nO Allah, all praise be to You for Your pleasant trials and deeds to us.\nوَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ عَلَىٰ الْاِسْلَامِ وَاتِّبَاعِ السُّنَّةِ\nWA LAKAL HAMDU A'LAL ISLAAMI WATTIBAA'IS SUNNAH\nAll praise be to You for my being Muslim and for my following the Prophet’s traditions.\nيَا رَبِّ كَمَا هَدَيْتَهُمْ لِدِيْنِكَ\nYAA RABBI KAMAA HADAYTAHUM LIDEENIK\nO my Lord, as You have guided them (i.e. the pious)\nوَعَلَّمْتَهُمْ كِتَابَكَ فَاهْدِنَا وَعَلِّمْنَا\nWA A'LLAMTAHUM KITAABAKA FAHDINAA WA A'LLIMNAA\nand taught them Your Book, (please) guide us and teach us.\nوَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ عَلَىٰ حُسْنِ بَلَائِكَ وَصُنْعِكَ عِنْدِيْ خَاصَّةً\nWA LAKAL HAMDU A'LAA HUSNI BALAA'IKA WA SUN'IKA I'NDEE KHAASSAH\nAll praise be to You for Your pleasant trials and deeds to me in private,\nكَمَا خَلَقْتَنِيْ فَاَحْسَنْتَ خَلْقِيْ\nKAMAA KHALAQTANEE FA-AHSANTA KHALQEE\nas You created me, gifted me an excellent form,\nوَعَلَّمْتَنِي فَاَحْسَنْتَ تَعْلِيْمِيْ\nWA A'LLAMTANEE FA-AHSANTA TA'LEEMEE\ntaught me, gifted me excellent erudition,\nوَهَدَيْتَنِي فَاَحْسَنْتَ هِدَايَتِيْ\nWA HADAYTANEE FA-AHSANTA HIDAAYATEE\nguided me, and gifted me excellent guidance.\nفَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ عَلَىٰ اِنْعَامِكَ عَلَيَّ قَدِيْمًا وَحَدِيثاً\nFALAKAL HAMDU A'LAA IN'AAMIKA A'LAYYA QADEEMAN WA HADEETHAA\nSo, all praise be to You for Your favors that You conferred upon me in the past and in the present.\nفَكَمْ مِنْ كَرْبٍ يَا سَيِّدِيْ قَدْ فَرَّجْتَهٗ\nFAKAM MIN KARBIN YAA SAYYIDEE QAD FARRAJTAH\nToo many are the agonies that You, my Master, relieved.\nوَكَمْ مِنْ غَمٍّ يَا سَيِّدِيْ قَدْ نَفَّسْتَهٗ\nWA KAM MIN GHAMMIN YAA SAYYIDEE QAD NAFFASTAH\nToo many are the distresses that You, my Master, eased.\nوَكَمْ مِنْ هَمٍّ يَا سَيِّدِيْ قَدْ كَشَفْتَهٗ\nWA KAM MIN HAMMIN YAA SAYYIDEE QAD KASHAFTAH\nToo many are the sufferings that You, my Master, alleviated.\nوَكَمْ مِنْ بَلَاءٍ يَا سَيِّدِيْ قَدْ صَرَفْتَهٗ\nWA KAM MIN BALAA'IN YAA SAYYIDEE QAD SARAFTAH\nToo many are the hardships from which You, my Master, saved me.\nوَكَمْ مِنْ عَيْبٍ يَا سَيِّدِيْ قَدْ سَتَرْتَهٗ\nWA KAM MIN A'YBIN YAA SAYYIDEE QAD SATARTAH\nToo many are the defects that You, my Master, covered.\nفَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ حَالٍ\nFALAKAL HAMDU A'LAA KULLI HAAL\nSo, all praise be to You for all conditions,\nفِيْ كُلِّ مَثْوَىٰ وَزَمَانٍ\nFEE KULLI MATHWAA WA ZAMAAN\nin every place and time,\nوَمُنْقَلَبٍ وَمَقَامٍ\nWA MUNQALABIN WA MAQAAM\nevery circumstance and situation,\nوَعَلَىٰ هٰذِهِ الْحَالِ وَكُلِّ حَالٍ\nWA A'LAA HAADHIHIL HAALI WA KULLI HAAL\nand for the current condition and all conditions.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْنِيْ مِنْ اَفْضَلِ عِبَادِكَ نَصِيْبًا\nALLAAHUMMAJ A'LNEE MIN AFDALI I'BAADIKA NASEEBAA\nO Allah, (please) shower upon me the best share of every good thing\nفِيْ هٰذَا الْيَوْمِ مِنْ خَيْرٍ تَقْسِمُهٗ\nFEE HAADHAL YAWMI MIN KHAYRIN TAQSIMUH\nthat You decide for Your servants on this day,\nاَوْ ضُرٍّ تَكْشِفُهٗ\nAW DURRIN TAKSHIFUH\nsuch as harm that You decide to hold off,\nاَوْ سُوْۤءٍ تَصْرِفُهٗ\nAW SOO'IN TASRIFUH\nevil that You decide to ward off,\nاَوْ بَلَاءٍ تَدْفَعُهٗ\nAW BALAA'IN TADFA'UH\nordeal that You decide to deter,\nاَوْ خَيْرٍ تَسُوْقُهٗ\nAW KHAYRIN TASOOQUH\ngrace that You decide to grant,\nاَوْ رَحْمَةٍ تَنْشُرُهَا\nAW RAHMATIN TANSHURUHAA\nitem of mercy that You decide to distribute,\nاَوْ عَافِيَةٍ تُلْبِسُهَا\nAW A'AFIYATIN TULBISUHAA\nand item of wellbeing that You decide to cover up (on one of Your servants),\nفَاِنَّكَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ\nFA-INNAKA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEER\nfor You verily have power over all things,\nوَبِيَدِكَ خَزَائِنُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْاَرْضِ\nWA BIYADIKA KHAZAA'INUS SAMAAWAATI WAL ARD\nin Your hands lie the hoards of the heavens and the earth,\nوَاَنْتَ الْوَاحِدُ الْكَرِيمُ الْمُعْطِي\nWA ANTAL WAAHIDUL KAREEMUL MU'TEE\nYou are verily the One, the All-generous, and the Best Bestower,\nالَّذِي لَا يُرَدُّ سَائِلُهٗ\nALLADHEE LAA YURADDU SAA'ILUH\nYou are the One Whose beseechers are not rejected,\nوَلَا يُخَيَّبُ اٰمِلُهٗ\nWA LAA YUKHAYYABU AAMILUH\nand You are the One Who never disappoint those who put hope in Him,\nوَلَا يَنْقُصُ نَائِلُهٗ\nWA LAA YANQUSU NAA'ILUH\nthe One Who is never influenced by the rewards that He bestows upon anyone,\nوَلَا يَنْفَدُ مَا عِنْدَهٗ\nWA LAA YANFADU MAA I'NDAH\nand the One Whose possessions never run out;\nبَلْ يَزْدَادُ كَثْرَةً وَطِيباً\nBAL YAZDAADU KATHRATAN WA TEEBAA\nrather, You always increase in quantity, excellent gift,\nوَعَطَاءً وَجُوداً\nWA A'TAA'AN WA JOODAA\nconferrals, and magnanimity.\nوَارْزُقْنِي مِنْ خَزَائِنِكَ الَّتِي لَا تَفْنَىٰ\nWARZUQNEE MIN KHAZAA'INIKAL LATEE LAA TAFNAA\n(Please) bestow upon me from Your hoards that never come to an end\nوَمِنْ رَحْمَتِكَ الْوَاسِعَةِ\nWA MIN RAHMATIKAL WAASI'AH\nand from Your expansive mercy.\nاِنَّ عَطَاءَكَ لَمْ يَكُنْ مَحْظُوْرًا\nINNA A'TAA'AKA LAM YAKUN MAHZOORAA\nYour conferral shall never be confined\nوَاَنْتَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ\nWA ANTA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEER\nand You have power over all things;\nبِرَحْمَتِكَ يَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِينَ\nBIRAHMATIKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nin the name of Your mercy; O most Merciful of all those who show mercy.",
    "Dua Ya Da'im al-Fadl\nNinth: It is recommended to repeat the following supplication ten times:\nيَا دَائِمَ الْفَضْلِ عَلَىٰ الْبَرِيَّةِ\nYAA DAA'IMAL FADLI A'LAL BARIYYAH\nO He Who is ever-Favorer on the beings!\nيَا بَاسِطَ الْيَدَيْنِ بِالْعَطِيَّةِ\nYAA BAASITAL YADAYNI BIL A'TIYYAH\nO He Who is openhandedly Bestower of gifts!\nيَا صَاحِبَ الْمَوَاهِبِ السَّنِيَّةِ\nYAA SAAHIBAL MAWAAHIBIS SANIYYAH\nO He Who is the Giver of sublime donations!\nصَلِّ عَلَىٰ مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِهٖ\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\nBless Muhammad and his Household,\nخَيْرِ الْوَرَىٰ سَجِيَّةً\nKHAYRIL WARAA SAJIYYAH\nthe best of all creatures in traits,\nوَاغْفِرْ لَنَا يَا ذَا الْعُلَىٰ\nWAGHFIR LANAA YAA DHAL U'LAA\nand forgive us, O Lord of Highness,\nفِي هٰذِهِ الْعَشِيَّةِ\nFEE HAADHIHIL A'SHIYYAH\nat this evening.\nThis honorable supplication is also recommended on the night of Eid al-Fitr and the night of Eid al-Adha.",
    "Between the Fajr Nafilah and the Fajr Prayer\nEleventh: In his book al-'Arus, Shaykh Ja'far ibn Ahmad al-Qummi has recorded that Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) said that one who repeats the following one hundred times between the supererogatory (nafilah) and obligatory prayers of Fajr will be given a house in Paradise by Almighty Allah:\nسُبْحَانَ رَبِّيَ الْعَظيمِ وَبِحَمْدِهٖ\nSUBHAANA RABBIYAL A'ZEEMI WA BIHAMDIH\nAll glory be to Allah, the All-great and with the Praising of Him;\nاَسْتَغْفِرُ اللَّهَ رَبِّيْ وَاَتُوبُ اِلَيْهِ\nASTAGHFIRULLAAHA RABBEE WA ATOOBU ILAYH\nI pray the forgiveness of Allah, my Lord, and I turn repentant to Him.",
    "Dua Before Dawn on Friday\nTwelfth: Shaykh al-Tusi, Sayyid Ibn Tawus and others have mentioned the following supplication, recommended on Friday nights just before dawn (Fajr):\nاَللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَىٰ مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِهٖ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\nO Allah, send blessings to Muhammad and his Household,\nوَهَبْ لِيَ الْغَدَاةَ رِضَاكَ\nWA HAB LIYAL GHADAATA RIDAAK\ngrant me Your satisfaction this very early morning,\nوَاَسْكِنْ قَلْبِيْ خَوْفَكَ\nWA ASKIN QALBEE KHAWFAK\nplace fear of You in my heart,\nوَاقْطَعْهُ عَمَّنْ سِوَاكَ\nWAQTA'HU A'MMAN SIWAAK\nand separate it from (leaning to) anyone other than You,\nحَتَّىٰ لَا اَرْجُوَ وَلَا اَخَافَ اِلَّا اِيَّاكَ\nHATTAA LAA ARJUWA WA LAA AKHAAFA ILLAA IYYAAK\nso that I will hope for and fear none save You.\nاَللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَىٰ مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِهٖ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\nO Allah, send blessings to Muhammad and his Household\nوَهَبْ لِيْ ثَبَاتَ الْيَقينِ\nWA HAB LEE THABAATAL YAQEEN\nand grant me resolute faith,\nوَمَحْضَ الْاِخْلَاصِ\nWA MAHDAL IKHLAAS\npure sincerity (to You),\nوَشَرَفَ التَّوْحيدِ\nWA SHARAFAT TAWHEED\nhonorable belief in (Your) oneness,\nوَدَوَامَ الْاِسْتِقَامَةِ\nWA DAWAAMAL ISTIQAAMAH\npersistent straightness,\nوَمَعْدِنَ الصَّبْرِ\nWA MA'DINAS SABR\nessential tolerance,\nوَالرِّضَا بِالْقَضَاءِ وَالْقَدَرِ\nWAR RIDAA BIL QADAA'I WAL QADAR\nand satisfaction with (Your) predetermination and decrees.\nيَا قَاضِيَ حَوَائِجِ السَّائِلينَ\nYAA QAADIYA HAWAA'IJIS SAA'ILEEN\nO He Who settles the needs of His beseechers;\nيَا مَنْ يَعْلَمُ مَا فِيْ ضَمِيْرِ الصَّامِتِينَ\nYAA MAN YA'LAMU MAA FEE DAMEERIS SAAMITEEN\nO He Who knows what is in the innermost of the silent;\nصَلِّ عَلَىٰ مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِهٖ\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\nsend blessings to Muhammad and his Household,\nوَاسْتَجِبْ دُعَائِي\nWASTAJIB DU'AA'EE\nrespond to my prayers,\nوَاغْفِرْ ذَنْبِيْ\nWAGHFIR DHANBEE\nforgive my sins,\nوَاَوْسِعْ رِزْقِيْ\nWA AWSI' RIZQEE\nexpand my means of livelihood,\nوَاقْضِ حَوَاۤئِجِيْ فِي نَفْسِيْ\nWAQDI HAWAA'IJEE FEE NAFSEE\nand settle the needs of myself\nوَاِخْوَانِي فِيْ دِيْنِيْ وَاَهْلِي\nWA IKHWAANEE FEE DEENEE WA AHLEE\nand my brethren-in-faith and my family members.\nاِلٰهِي طُمُوْحُ الْاٰمَالِ قَدْ خَابَتْ اِلَّا لَدَيْكَ\nILAAHEE TUMOOHUL AAMAALI QAD KHAABAT ILLAA LADAYK\nO Allah, all ambitions of expectations are disappointed except those addressed to You,\nوَمَعَاكِفُ الْهِمَمِ قَدْ تَعَطَّلَتْ اِلَّا عَلَيْكَ\nWA MA'AAKIFUL HIMAMI QAD TA'ATTALAT ILLAA A'LAYK\nall resolute determinations are paralyzed except those relied upon You,\nوَمَذَاهِبُ الْعُقُولِ قَدْ سَمَتْ اِلَّا اِلَيْكَ\nWA MADHAAHIBUL U'QOOLI QAD SAMAT ILLAA ILAYK\nand all reason-based tendencies are wasted except those directed to You.\nفَاَنْتَ الرَّجَاءُ وَاِلَيْكَ الْمُلْتَجَاُ\nFA-ANTAR RAJAA'U WA ILAYKAL MULTAJA'\nSo, You are the ultimate hope and to You is the resort.\nيَا اَكْرَمَ مَقْصُوْدٍ وَاَجْوَدَ مَسْؤُولٍ\nYAA AKRAMA MAQSOODIN WA AJWADA MAS'OOL\nO He Who is the noblest objective and the most magnanimous desired,\nهَرَبْتُ اِلَيْكَ بِنَفْسِيْ\nHARABTU ILAYKA BINAFSEE\nI am fleeing to You from myself.\nيَا مَلْجَاَ الْهَارِبِينَ بِاَثْقَالِ الذُّنُوبِ\nYAA MALJA'AL HAARIBEENA BI-ATHQAALIDH DHUNOOB\nO shelter of those who flee overburdened with the heavy loads of sins,\nاَحْمِلُهَا عَلَىٰ ظَهْرِيْ\nAHMILUHAA A'LAA ZAHREE\ncarrying my sins on my back,\nلَا اَجِدُ لِيْ اِلَيْكَ شَافِعاً\nLAA AJIDU LEE ILAYKA SHAAFI'AA\nI cannot find any interceder for me\nسِوَىٰ مَعْرِفَتِيْ بِاَنَّكَ اَقْرَبُ مَنْ رَجَاهُ الطَّالِبُونَ\nSIWAA MA'RIFATEE BI-ANNAKA AQRABU MAN RAJAAHUT TAALIBOON\nexcept that I know for sure that You are the nearest of all those who are hoped by beseechers\nوَاَمَّلَ مَا لَدَيْهِ الرَّاغِبُونَ\nWA AMMALA MAA LADAYHIR RAAGHIBOON\nand of all those whose donations are expected by the desirous.\nيَا مَنْ فَتَقَ الْعُقُولَ بِمَعْرِفَتِهٖ\nYAA MAN FATAQAL U'QOOLA BIMA'RIFATIH\nO He Who has split the intellects on the recognition of Him,\nوَاَطْلَقَ الْاَلْسُنَ بِحَمْدِهٖ\nWA ATLAQAL ALSUNA BIHAMDIH\nmade tongues articulate with the praising of Him\nوَجَعَلَ مَا امْتَنَّ بِهٖ عَلَىٰ عِبَادِهٖ فِي كِفَاءٍ لِتَاْدِيَةِ حَقِّهٖ\nWA JA'ALA MAM TANNA BIHEE A'LAA I'BAADIHEE FEE KIFAA'IN LITA'DIYATI HAQQIH\nand made that which He has conferred upon His servants enough means for the fulfillment of their duties towards Him;\nصَلِّ عَلَىٰ مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِهٖ\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\n(please) send blessings to Muhammad and his Household,\nوَلَا تَجْعَلْ لِّلشَّيْطَانِ عَلَىٰ عَقْلِيْ سَبِيْلًا\nWA LAA TAJ'AL LISH SHAYTAANI A'LAA A'QLEE SABEELAA\ndo not give Satan any way (of success) over my reason,\nوَلَا لِلْبَاطِلِ عَلَىٰ عَمَلِيْ دَلِيْلًا.\nWA LAA LIL BAATILI A'LAA A'MALEE DALEELAA\nand do not give wrongness a way to reach my deeds.",
    "Prayer of Imam al-Mahdi (a.t.f.s.) on Friday Night\nQuoting the book Kunuz al-Najah by Shaykh al-Tabrisi, the author of al-Najm al-Thaqib mentions the following statement from the Holy Region (i.e. Imam al-Mahdi, a.t.f.s.): \"Whoever has a request to be granted urgently by Almighty Allah may bathe himself after midnight on a Friday night, go to his place of prayer and offer a two-unit prayer. In the first unit he recites Surah al-Fatihah, and when he reaches this verse he repeats it one hundred times:\nاِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَاِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِيْنُ\nIYYAAKA NA'BUDU WA IYYAAKA NASTA'EEN\nYou alone do we worship, and You alone do we ask for help.\nHe then completes the Surah and recites [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) once. In the ruku' of each unit he repeats the following seven times:\nسُبْحَانَ رَبِّيَ الْعَظِيْمِ وَبِحَمْدِهِ\nSUBHAANA RABBIYAL A'ZEEMI WA BIHAMDIH\nGlory be to my Lord, the Great, and praise belongs to Him.\nAnd in each of the two prostrations of each unit he repeats the following seven times:\nسُبْحَانَ رَبِّيَ الْاَعْلٰى وَبِحَمْدِهِ\nSUBHAANA RABBIYAL A'LAA WA BIHAMDIH\nGlory be to my Lord, the Most High, and praise belongs to Him.\nUpon finishing the prayer he says the following supplication; if he does, Almighty Allah will certainly grant his request, unless it involves cutting off relations with his relatives:\nاللَّهُمَّ اِنْ اَطَعْتُكَ فَالْمَحْمَدَةُ لَكَ\nALLAAHUMMA IN ATA'TUKA FAL MAHMADATU LAK\nO Allah, if I obey You, then praise is due to You,\nوَاِنْ عَصَيْتُكَ فَالْحُجَّةُ لَكَ\nWA IN A'SAYTUKA FAL HUJJATU LAK\nand if I disobey You, then the argument is Yours.\nمِنْكَ الرَّوْحُ وَمِنْكَ الْفَرَجُ\nMINKAR RAWHU WA MINKAL FARAJ\nFrom You comes ease, and from You comes relief.\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ اَنْعَمَ وَشَكَرَ\nSUBHAANA MAN AN'AMA WA SHAKAR\nGlory be to Him Who bestows favor and is grateful!\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ قَدَّرَ وَغَفَرَ\nSUBHAANA MAN QADDARA WA GHAFAR\nGlory be to Him Who decrees and forgives!\nاللَّهُمَّ اِنْ كُنْتُ عَصَيْتُكَ\nALLAAHUMMA IN KUNTU A'SAYTUK\nO Allah, if I have disobeyed You,\nفَاِنِّي قَدْ اَطَعْتُكَ فِي اَحَبِّ الْاَشْيَاءِ اِلَيْكَ\nFA-INNEE QAD ATA'TUKA FEE AHABBIL ASHYAA'I ILAYK\nI have obeyed You in the thing most beloved to You,\nوَهُوَ الْاِيمَانُ بِكَ\nWA HUWAL EEMAANU BIK\nwhich is faith in You.\nلَمْ اَتَّخِذْ لَكَ وَلَدًا\nLAM ATTAKHIDH LAKA WALADAA\nI have not taken a son for You,\nوَلَمْ اَدْعُ لَكَ شَرِيكًا\nWA LAM AD'U LAKA SHAREEKAA\nnor have I called on any partner besides You;\nمَنّاً مِنْكَ بِهٖ عَلَيَّ\nMANNAN MINKA BIHEE A'LAYY\nthis is Your favor upon me,\nلَا مَنّاً مِنِّي بِهٖ عَلَيْكَ\nLAA MANNAN MINNEE BIHEE A'LAYK\nnot my favor upon You.\nوَقَدْ عَصَيْتُكَ يَا اِلٰهِي عَلَى غَيْرِ وَجْهِ الْمُكَابَرَةِ\nWA QAD A'SAYTUKA YAA ILAAHEE A'LAA GHAYRI WAJHIL MUKAABARAH\nI have disobeyed You, my God, not out of arrogance,\nوَلَا الْخُرُوجِ عَنْ عُبُودِيَّتِكَ\nWA LAL KHUROOJI A'N U'BOODIYYATIK\nnor to depart from servitude to You,\nوَلَا الْجُحُودِ لِرُبُوبِيَّتِكَ\nWA LAL JUHOODI LIRUBOOBIYYATIK\nnor to deny Your Lordship;\nوَلٰكِنْ اَطَعْتُ هَوَايَ\nWA LAAKIN ATA'TU HAWAAY\nrather, I followed my desires,\nوَاَزَلَّنِي الشَّيْطَانُ\nWA AZALLANISH SHAYTAAN\nand Satan made me slip.\nفَلَكَ الْحُجَّةُ عَلَيَّ وَالْبَيَانُ\nFALAKAL HUJJATU A'LAYYA WAL BAYAAN\nSo Yours is the argument against me, and the clear proof.\nفَاِنْ تُعَذِّبْنِي فَبِذُنُوبِي غَيْرَ ظَالِمٍ\nFA-IN TU'ADHDHIBNEE FABIDHUNOOBEE GHAYRA ZAALIM\nIf You punish me, it is for my sins, and You do not wrong me;\nوَاِنْ تَغْفِرْ لِي وَتَرْحَمْنِي فَاِنَّكَ جَوَادٌ كَرِيمٌ\nWA IN TAGHFIR LEE WA TARHAMNEE FA-INNAKA JAWAADUN KAREEM\nand if You forgive me and have mercy on me, then You are the Magnanimous, the Generous.\nHe then repeats the following as long as one breath lasts:\nيَا كَرِيْمُ يَا كَرِيْمُ\nYAA KAREEMU YAA KAREEM\nO Generous! O Generous!\nThen he continues:\nيَا آمِنًا مِنْ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ\nYAA AAMINAN MIN KULLI SHAY'\nO He Who is safe from everything,\nوَكُلُّ شَيْءٍ مِنْكَ خَائِفٌ حَذِرٌ\nWA KULLU SHAY'IN MINKA KHAA'IFUN HADHIR\nwhile everything fears You and is wary of You!\nاَسْاَلُكَ بِاَمْنِكَ مِنْ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ\nAS'ALUKA BI-AMNIKA MIN KULLI SHAY'\nI ask You by Your being safe from everything\nوَخَوْفِ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ مِنْكَ\nWA KHAWFI KULLI SHAY'IN MINK\nand by everything's fear of You\nاَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nAN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nto send blessings upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَاَنْ تُعْطِيَنِي اَمَانًا لِنَفْسِي\nWA AN TU'TIYANEE AMAANAN LINAFSEE\nto grant me security for myself,\nوَاَهْلِي وَمَالِي وَوَلَدِي\nWA AHLEE WA MAALEE WA WALADEE\nmy family, my property, my children\nوَسَائِرِ مَا اَنْعَمْتَ بِهٖ عَلَيَّ\nWA SAA'IRI MAA AN'AMTA BIHEE A'LAYY\nand all the favors You have bestowed upon me,\nحَتَّى لَا اَخَافَ\nHATTAA LAA AKHAAF\nso that I fear no one\nوَلَا اَحْذَرَ مِنْ شَيْءٍ اَبَدًا\nWA LAA AHDHARA MIN SHAY'IN ABADAA\nand am wary of nothing, ever.\nاِنَّكَ عَلَى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ\nINNAKA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEER\nVerily, You have power over all things.\nوَحَسْبُنَا اللَّهُ وَنِعْمَ الْوَكِيلُ\nWA HASBUNALLAAHU WA NI'MAL WAKEEL\nAllah is sufficient for us, and He is the best Guardian.\nيَا كَافِيَ اِبْرَاهِيمَ نَمْرُودَ\nYAA KAAFIYA IBRAAHEEMA NAMROOD\nO He Who sufficed Abraham against Nimrod!\nوَيَا كَافِيَ مُوسَى فِرْعَوْنَ\nWA YAA KAAFIYA MOOSAA FIR'AWN\nO He Who sufficed Moses against Pharaoh!\nاَسْاَلُكَ اَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nAS'ALUKA AN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nI ask You to send blessings upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَاَنْ تَكْفِيَنِيْ شَرَّ فُلَانِ بْنِ فُلَانٍ\nWA AN TAKFIYANEE SHARRA FULAANIBNI FULAAN\nand to spare me the evil of so-and-so, son of so-and-so.\nHe then mentions by name, with his father's name, the one whose harm he fears, and asks Almighty Allah to repel his harm and save him from his evil; Almighty Allah will certainly do so, if He wills. Then he prostrates, submits his request, and beseeches Almighty Allah earnestly and sincerely. If any believing man or woman offers this prayer and says this supplication, the doors of the heavens will be opened for them, their requests will be granted, and their prayer will be answered at once, whatever it may be. This is one of the favors of Almighty Allah upon us and upon the people.\"\nRadi al-Din Hasan ibn al-Fadl, the son of Shaykh al-Tabrisi, has also reported this prayer in Makarim al-Akhlaq with small differences in the supplication: he adds qad (surely) after kuntu, ahadan (anyone) after akhafa, and as'aluka (I beseech You) after fir'awna."
